.TH CHTTPCLIENT_RESP_HEADER_COUNT 3 "2026-09-29" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_resp_header_count \- count the lines of a response header
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

size_t chttpclient_resp_header_count(const chttpcli_response *resp,
                                     const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function returns how many lines of the response header block carry
the given name, compared without regard to case. Each such line counts
once whatever its value, an empty value included.

Use it together with chttpclient_resp_header_at to read every
occurrence of a header that a server can send more than once, such as
Set-Cookie.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
resp  The response to query. It can be NULL, in which case the
      function returns 0.
name  The header name. It can be NULL, in which case the function
      returns 0.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The number of lines with that name, or 0 if there are none. A response
from a streaming request keeps no headers, so it always gives 0.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Only the response's header block counts. A trailer field of a chunked
body is not a response header and is never counted here.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
size_t n = chttpclient_resp_header_count(resp, "Set-Cookie");
for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++)
    printf("cookie: %s\\n",
           chttpclient_resp_header_at(resp, "Set-Cookie", i));
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_at (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_header (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_free (3)
